      "answer": "$(\\alpha,\\beta)=(45^\\circ,18.4^\\circ)$ or $(108.4^\\circ,135^\\circ)$.",
      "official_mark_scheme_text": "Use the correct $\\tan(A+B)$ formula and obtain an equation in $\\tan\\alpha$ and $\\tan\\beta$. M1. Substitute throughout for $\\tan\\alpha$ or $\\tan\\beta$. M1. Obtain $3\\tan^2\\beta+2\\tan\\beta-1=0$ or $\\tan^2\\alpha+2\\tan\\alpha-3=0$, or equivalent. A1. Solve a three-term quadratic and find an angle. M1. Obtain $\\alpha=45^\\circ$, $\\beta=18.4^\\circ$. A1; accept $\\pi/4$ or $0.785,0.322$. Obtain $\\alpha=108.4^\\circ$, $\\beta=135^\\circ$. A1; accept $1.89,3\\pi/4$ or $2.36$. Guidance: an answer in radians is at most A1 A0 or vice versa; ignore answers outside $[0^\\circ,180^\\circ]$. SC: if A0 A0, allow B1 for both $\\alpha$ values or both $\\beta$ values. Total 6.",
